# E2E Seed Schema Alignment

E2e suites seed Postgres with inline `dataSource.query(...)` after `truncatePostgres`. **Table and column names must match Flyway migrations**, not mobile API route names or TypeScript DTO fields.

## Source-of-truth order

Before writing any `INSERT`:

1. Existing e2e in the same domain (e.g. `test/bookings-payment.e2e-spec.ts`)
2. Matching file under `seed/` — see [`.cursor/seed-directory.md`](../seed-directory.md)
3. `db/migrations/V*.sql` for the table definition

Never guess names from API paths (`/categories` ≠ table `categories`).

## Common traps

| Wrong (invented) | Correct (Flyway) |
|---|---|
| `categories` | `service_categories` |
| `catalog_services` without `target_gender` | `target_gender` is NOT NULL — include it |
| `sort_order` on `service_categories` | `sort_order` exists on `shop_services`, not categories |

## Bad vs good

```sql
-- BAD — relation "categories" does not exist
INSERT INTO categories (id, name, slug, sort_order) VALUES (...);

-- GOOD — matches V6 + bookings-payment.e2e-spec.ts
INSERT INTO service_categories (id, slug, name, status)
  VALUES ($1, 'hair-e2e', 'Hair', 'active');
INSERT INTO catalog_services (id, category_id, name, target_gender, is_active)
  VALUES ($1, $2, 'Classic Cut', 'male', true);
```

## Checklist before finishing e2e work

- [ ] Every `INSERT` table name exists in a Flyway migration
- [ ] Column list matches migration (required NOT NULL columns included)
- [ ] Pattern copied from working e2e or `seed/*.sql` where possible
- [ ] `pnpm run test:e2e:prep` then run the single spec: `pnpm exec jest --config ./test/jest-e2e.json --runInBand test/<file>.e2e-spec.ts`

A failed `beforeAll` seed kills **every** test in the suite — verify seed SQL first.
